# Smart Home IoT Project — Technical Walkthrough

## Architecture Overview

```
ESP32 (MicroPython)
  ├── Thread 1: radar.py — servo sweep + HC-SR04 (always running)
  ├── Thread 2: _cmd_thread — polls /command/pending every 300ms
  └── Main loop — sensor POST every 400ms + health ping every 250s

FastAPI Backend (Python)
  ├── POST /sensor-data     ← ESP32 pushes buffered radar data
  ├── POST /command         ← Browser sends LED/protect commands
  ├── GET  /command/pending ← ESP32 polls (Thread 2)
  ├── WS   /ws             ← Browser subscribes for real-time updates
  └── GET  /stats/*         ← MongoDB analytics queries

Browser (Vanilla JS + Bootstrap 5)
  ├── ws.js        — persistent WebSocket, auto-reconnect
  ├── radar.js     — 60fps canvas, scan history, ping-pong extrapolation
  ├── leds.js      — optimistic toggle with WS confirmation
  ├── sensors.js   — flame/gate/protect-mode display
  └── stats.html   — separate analytics page (MongoDB data)
```

